    "historical_decision": "Kingdom of Yugoslavia, Democratic Federal Yugoslavia, Federal People's Republic of Yugoslavia and Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia are successive constitutional/name phases of one continuing international Yugoslav state identity. The Archives of Yugoslavia states that the AVNOJ constitutional rupture suspended internal continuity with the Kingdom but did not interrupt Yugoslavia's international legal continuity as a subject of international law. It records that on 7 March 1945 the Royal Yugoslav Government and NKOJ were dissolved and replaced by one provisional government of Democratic Federal Yugoslavia. The U.N. treats the former Yugoslavia/SFRY as an original Member from 1945 until dissolution. Federal Republic of Yugoslavia (1992) is not present in current Production and is excluded from this merge because U.N. Security Council resolution 777 states that the SFRY had ceased to exist and FRY could not automatically continue its membership.",
    "activity_rule": "Peter II's kingship remains a distinct King Activity, while Tito's Prime Minister and President offices remain distinct roles. Official-name or constitutional-form transitions within the same state must not split Tito's continuous tenure in the same role.",
    "designation_rule": "Preserve Kingdom of Yugoslavia as temporal state_form from the 3 October 1929 naming/constitutional phase through the day before the 29 November 1945 abolition of the monarchy. Preserve Democratic Federal Yugoslavia as temporal official_name from formation of the united provisional government on 7 March 1945 through 28 November 1945. Preserve Federal People's Republic of Yugoslavia as temporal official_name from proclamation on 29 November 1945 through 6 April 1963, the day before the 1963 Constitution renamed the state the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia. The partial 1945 overlap of Kingdom state_form and DFY official_name is intentional: royal legal form persisted under a Regency while the united provisional DFY government operated until the Constituent Assembly abolished the monarchy."
  },
